course: dictionary
lesson: 9814
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Swear has three main ones, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Ava's gran chats to her tomatoes every morning and swears they grow faster for it.» Here swear means she says it is really true, not that she uses bad words.
explain: The first meaning is to use rude or bad words, the kind that can upset people. «Swear words» are the words we do not say at school or at a friend's home. Manners lessons teach that swearing can hurt others, so always think about who is listening.
explain: The second meaning is to make a serious promise. In court, a witness must «swear to tell the truth», and that promise is taken very seriously. «I swear» is a way people say that something is really true. If someone is promising, it is this meaning.
explain: The third meaning is to swear someone in, which means making them promise to do a job honestly. Leaders are «sworn in», and judges take an oath before they start. Stories use it too: a character may «swear revenge» or be one of someone's «sworn enemies».
fact: Swear is a verb: swear, swears, swore, sworn, swearing.
fact: «Swear» can mean to use rude words, to say something is really true, or to make a serious promise.
fact: «Swear to tell the truth» means promising that what you say in court is true.
fact: «Sworn in» means officially promised to do a job honestly, like a new leader.
fact: In UK courts, people may swear on a holy book or make a non-religious affirmation instead. Lying in court is a crime called perjury.
exercise: «Ava's gran swears her tomatoes grow faster when she chats to them.» What does swears mean here? | Uses rude words | Shouts at them | Forgets to water them | *Says something is really true
exercise: The witness must «swear to tell the whole truth» in court. What does swear mean? | To use bad words | To tell rude jokes | *To make a serious promise
exercise: Find and copy the past tense of swear in this sentence: «He swore he would help.» | sworn | swear | swearing | *swore
test: The mayor was «sworn in» on Monday. What does sworn in mean? | Given a new car | Thrown out of the office | *Officially promised to do the job honestly | Told to be quiet
test: Kieran swears «rottweilers are killers», but then he meets a gentle one. What does swears mean? | Uses rude words | Runs away from it | Counts to ten | *Says something is really true, though he is wrong
exam: Which sentence uses swear to mean use rude words? | «She swore to keep her promise to me.» | «The judge swore in the new mayor.» | *«Some people swear when they are angry, and it can upset others.» | «I swear the cake is the best I have ever tasted.»
